{title: 176 - Hail the Day That Sees Him Rise}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #176 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 176}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Hail the [Dm]day that [Am]sees [Bb]Him [C]rise, [Am]Allelu [F/C]ia!
[Bb]Glo-rious [F]to His native [Dm]skies; [Am]Allelu [C]ia!
[Am]Christ, [Gm]awhile [F/C]to [Bb]mortals [F]giv'n, Alleluia!
[Bb]Enters [Gm]now the [C]highest [F]heav'n! Allelu [C]ia!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]There the [Dm]glorious [Bb]triumph [C]waits; [Am]Alleluia!
[Bb]Lift your [F]heads, eternal [Dm]gates! [Bb]Alleluia!
[Am]Wide [Gm]unfold [F/C]the radiant scene; Alleluia!
[Bb]Take the [Gm]King of [C]glory [F]in! Alleluia!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]See! He [Dm]lifts His [Bb]hands above; [Gm]Alleluia!
[Bb]See! [F]He shows the [Dm]prints of [Am]love: [Bb]Alleluia!
[Am]Hark! [Gm]His [F]gracious lips [Bb]bestow, [F]Alleluia!
[Bb]Blessings [Gm]on His [C]Church [F]below. Alleluia!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Lord beyond [Dm]our [Am]mortal [C]sight, [Am]Alleluia!
[Bb]Raise [F]our hearts to [Dm]reach Thy [Am]height, [Bb]Alleluia!
[Am]There [Gm]Thy [F]face unclouded see, Alleluia!
[Bb]Find our [Gm]heav'n of [C]heav'ns [F]in Thee. Alleluia!
{end_of_verse}
